Sec. 60001 rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out section 132 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7432), the Clean Heavy-Duty Vehicles program. This eliminates any remaining unspent appropriations for that program.

Sec. 60002 repeals section 134 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7434), the Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund, and rescinds all unobligated balances made available under that section as in effect on the day before enactment. This abolishes the fund and recovers unspent amounts.

Sec. 60003 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60104 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067), the diesel emissions reductions program. This recovers unspent funds for that program.

Sec. 60004 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60105 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067), funding to address air pollution. This recovers unspent appropriations for that purpose.

Sec. 60005 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60106 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2069), funding to address air pollution at schools. This recovers unspent funds for that program.

Sec. 60006 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 135 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7435), the Low Emissions Electricity Program. This recovers unspent appropriations for that program.

Sec. 60007 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60108 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2070), funding related to section 211(o) of the Clean Air Act. This recovers unspent funds for that purpose.

Sec. 60008 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60109 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071), funding for implementation of the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act. This recovers unspent appropriations for that implementation.

Sec. 60009 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60110 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071), funding for enforcement technology and public information. This recovers unspent funds for that purpose.

Sec. 60010 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60111 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2072), funding for greenhouse gas corporate reporting. This recovers unspent appropriations for that reporting.

Sec. 60011 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60112 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2072), funding for environmental product declaration assistance. This recovers unspent funds for that assistance.

Sec. 60012 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out subsections (a) and (b) of section 136 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7436), the methane emissions and waste reduction incentive program for petroleum and natural gas systems, and amends section 136(g) to extend the program period from calendar year 2024 to calendar year 2034. This recovers unspent funds while extending the program's authorization by ten years.

Sec. 60013 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 137 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7437), funding for greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants. This recovers unspent appropriations for those plans and grants.

Sec. 60014 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60115 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2077), funding for Environmental Protection Agency efficient, accurate, and timely reviews. This recovers unspent funds for that purpose.

Sec. 60015 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60116 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2077), funding for low-embodied carbon labeling for construction materials. This recovers unspent appropriations for that labeling.

Sec. 60016 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 138 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7438), funding for environmental and climate justice block grants. This recovers unspent funds for those grants.

Sec. 60017 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60301 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079), funding for ESA recovery plans. This recovers unspent appropriations for those plans.

Sec. 60018 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60401 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079), funding for environmental and climate data collection. This recovers unspent funds for that collection.

Sec. 60019 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 177 of title 23, United States Code, the Neighborhood Access and Equity Grant Program. This recovers unspent funds for that grant program.

Sec. 60020 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60502 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), funding for Federal building assistance. This recovers unspent appropriations for that assistance.

Sec. 60021 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60503 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), funding for low-carbon materials for Federal buildings. This recovers unspent funds for that purpose.

Sec. 60022 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60504 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), funding for GSA emerging and sustainable technologies. This recovers unspent appropriations for those technologies.

Sec. 60023 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 178 of title 23, United States Code, environmental review implementation funds. This recovers unspent funds for that purpose.

Sec. 60024 rescinds the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 179 of title 23, United States Code, low-carbon transportation materials grants. This recovers unspent funds for those grants.

Sec. 60025 appropriates $256,657,000 for fiscal year 2025, available until September 30, 2029, for capital repair, restoration, maintenance backlog, and security structures of the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts building and site, with not more than 3 percent usable for administrative costs. This provides new funding for the Center's capital needs.

Sec. 60026 amends title I of the National Environmental Policy Act of 1969 to add section 112, allowing project sponsors to opt in to paying fees for environmental reviews. A sponsor submits a project description and declaration to the Council on Environmental Quality, which within 15 days provides notice of the fee amount, set at 125 percent of anticipated preparation costs (or 125 percent of anticipated supervision/preparation costs if the sponsor prepares the review under section 107(f)); upon payment, an environmental assessment must be completed within 180 days and an environmental impact statement within 1 year of the notice of intent. [end of text]


